LN(1)                          User Commands                           LN(1)

NAME
    ln - give a file a second name

SYNOPSIS
    ln OLD NEW

DESCRIPTION
    Make NEW a hard link to the regular file OLD. Both names refer to one
    file: a write through either is seen through the other, and the data
    lasts until the last name is removed. NEW is created in the working
    directory.

    Only a regular file can be linked, and you must own it. A link names
    its source by inode, which a directory capability never does, so a
    shell that walks by capability is refused; there is no cross-directory
    link yet.

SEE ALSO
    rm(1), stat(1)
